{"title":"Career Roadmap · Regional Planner","role":"Regional Planner","summary":"A Regional Planner plans development across cities, towns, rural areas and larger geographic regions. Unlike an urban planner who may focus primarily on a city or neighbourhood, a regional planner looks at the relationships between settlements, transportation, housing, employment, agriculture, industry, infrastructure, natural resources and the environment.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Plan (Bachelor of Planning)","Course":"Urban & Regional Planning"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Regional Planner plans development across cities, towns, rural areas and larger geographic regions. Unlike an urban planner who may focus primarily on a city or neighbourhood, a regional planner looks at the relationships between settlements, transportation, housing, employment, agriculture, industry, infrastructure, natural resources and the environment."},{"type":"p","text":"The role is highly analytical and combines:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Spatial planning"},{"text":"Regional economics"},{"text":"Demography"},{"text":"GIS"},{"text":"Transportation"},{"text":"Land-use planning"},{"text":"Infrastructure planning"},{"text":"Environmental planning"},{"text":"Geographic data analysis"},{"text":"Policy and governance"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Typical responsibilities include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Preparing regional development plans"},{"text":"Analysing population and migration patterns"},{"text":"Planning settlement hierarchies"},{"text":"Studying regional infrastructure requirements"},{"text":"Mapping land-use changes"},{"text":"Planning transport corridors"},{"text":"Identifying growth centres"},{"text":"Supporting metropolitan/regional plans"},{"text":"Evaluating development proposals"},{"text":"Conducting socio-economic surveys"},{"text":"Preparing spatial strategies"},{"text":"Supporting g